---
import AsterLayout from "../../layouts/AsterLayout.astro";
import { ASTER_DEX_ID, AUTHORS, PERSON_ID, SITE_URL } from "../../entity";
import { buildAsterPageGraph, buildBreadcrumbs } from "../../lib/schema";
import { ASTER_DOCS, ASTER_LAST_VERIFIED } from "../../data/aster";

const url = `${SITE_URL}/aster-dex/shield-mode/`;
const description =
  "Shield Mode explained: the AMM-style Aster interface, built-in privacy, the 0.03% flat fee and 15–20% profit share, and the risks of trading against a pool.";

const articleNode = {
  "@type": "TechArticle",
  "@id": `${url}#article`,
  headline: "Shield Mode",
  alternativeHeadline: "Shield Mode: Aster's AMM-style perpetual interface",
  name: "Shield Mode: Aster's AMM-style perpetual interface",
  description,
  url,
  mainEntityOfPage: url,
  inLanguage: "en",
  datePublished: "2026-11-24",
  dateModified: ASTER_LAST_VERIFIED,
  author: { "@id": AUTHORS.kirsty.id },
  editor: { "@id": AUTHORS.maksim.id },
  publisher: { "@id": PERSON_ID },
  isPartOf: { "@id": `${SITE_URL}/aster-dex/#collection` },
  articleSection: "Trading modes",
  about: [
    { "@id": ASTER_DEX_ID },
    { "@type": "Thing", name: "Automated market maker" },
    { "@type": "Thing", name: "Perpetual futures" },
  ],
  citation: [
    { "@type": "CreativeWork", name: "Shield Mode", url: `${ASTER_DOCS}trading/shield-mode` },
    { "@type": "CreativeWork", name: "Shield Mode fees & specs", url: `${ASTER_DOCS}trading/shield-mode/fees-and-specs` },
  ],
};

const breadcrumbs = buildBreadcrumbs(`${url}#breadcrumbs`, [
  { name: "Home", url: `${SITE_URL}/` },
  { name: "Aster DEX", url: `${SITE_URL}/aster-dex/` },
  { name: "Shield Mode", url },
]);

const graph = buildAsterPageGraph([articleNode, breadcrumbs]);
---

<AsterLayout
  title="Shield Mode — Aster's AMM-Style Perpetuals Explained | Maksim Sokal"
  description={description}
  canonical={url}
  graph={graph}
  trail={[{ label: "Shield Mode" }]}
  modified={new Date(ASTER_LAST_VERIFIED)}
>
  <header class="space-y-5 max-w-3xl">
    <span class="text-xs font-mono text-sky-400 uppercase tracking-widest block">Trading Modes</span>
    <h1 class="font-display font-medium text-3xl md:text-4xl text-slate-100 tracking-tight leading-tight">
      Shield Mode
    </h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
      Shield Mode is Aster's simplified, AMM-style perpetual interface. There is no order book to manage: you choose a
      market, a size and a leverage, and the pool is the counterparty. Privacy is built into the flow rather than
      switched on afterwards.
    </p>
    <p class="text-[11px] font-mono text-slate-400">
      Verified <time datetime={ASTER_LAST_VERIFIED}>{ASTER_LAST_VERIFIED}</time> ·{" "}
      <a href={`${ASTER_DOCS}trading/shield-mode`} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-sky-400 hover:text-sky-300">official Shield Mode docs</a>
    </p>
  </header>

  <section class="space-y-4" aria-labelledby="model-heading">
    <h2 id="model-heading" class="font-display font-medium text-xl text-slate-100 tracking-tight">How the model differs</h2>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
      <div class="bg-brand-900/35 border border-[#1e293b]/60 rounded-xl p-5 space-y-2">
        <h3 class="font-display text-sm text-slate-100">Order book (Pro mode)</h3>
        <p class="text-xs text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
          You post or take liquidity at a price. Execution depends on depth, queue position and order type. Maker and
          taker fees apply.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-brand-900/35 border border-[#1e293b]/60 rounded-xl p-5 space-y-2">
        <h3 class="font-display text-sm text-slate-100">Shield Mode (AMM)</h3>
        <p class="text-xs text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
          The pool quotes the trade. Execution is immediate, slippage is dynamic, and the pool takes the other side.
          Fewer decisions, different cost structure.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-4" aria-labelledby="cost-heading">
    <h2 id="cost-heading" class="font-display font-medium text-xl text-slate-100 tracking-tight">What it costs</h2>
    <div class="bg-brand-900/35 border border-[#1e293b]/60 rounded-xl p-6 space-y-3">
      <div class="flex items-center justify-between text-xs">
        <span class="text-slate-400">Flat fee</span>
        <span class="text-slate-100 font-mono">0.03%</span>
      </div>
      <div class="flex items-center justify-between text-xs">
        <span class="text-slate-400">Profit share on winning positions</span>
        <span class="text-slate-100 font-mono">15–20%</span>
      </div>
      <div class="flex items-center justify-between text-xs">
        <span class="text-slate-400">Profit share on losing positions</span>
        <span class="text-slate-100 font-mono">0%</span>
      </div>
      <p class="text-[11px] text-amber-300/90 leading-relaxed pt-2">
        Aster was running a limited-time zero-fee promotion on opening and closing at the time of verification. A
        promotion is not a permanent fee model; assume the 0.03% + profit share returns.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-4" aria-labelledby="slippage-heading">
    <h2 id="slippage-heading" class="font-display font-medium text-xl text-slate-100 tracking-tight">Dynamic slippage is the hidden variable</h2>
    <p class="text-xs text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
      Shield Mode determines slippage from the liquidity of the underlying assets and the pool's open interest. Unlike a
      fixed 0.01% on BTC/USD in Degen Mode, the number is not known until execution. Large orders in thin markets can pay
      significantly more than the headline fee.
    </p>
    <p class="text-xs text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
      This matters for position sizing. A strategy that is profitable at 0.03% can be unprofitable at the realised
      slippage. Model the fill, not the fee schedule.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6" aria-labelledby="fit-heading">
    <div class="space-y-3">
      <h2 id="fit-heading" class="font-display font-medium text-lg text-slate-100 tracking-tight">Shield Mode suits</h2>
      <ul class="space-y-2 text-xs text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
        <li>Traders who want a position without managing orders.</li>
        <li>Users who value privacy in the execution flow.</li>
        <li>Smaller accounts that want a lower barrier to entry and higher available leverage.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="space-y-3">
      <h2 class="font-display font-medium text-lg text-slate-100 tracking-tight">It does not suit</h2>
      <ul class="space-y-2 text-xs text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
        <li>Limit-order strategies that depend on queue position.</li>
        <li>Traders who need a known fill price before sending.</li>
        <li>Anyone who cannot absorb the loss of the full margin.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-3" aria-labelledby="risk-heading">
    <h2 id="risk-heading" class="font-display font-medium text-lg text-slate-100 tracking-tight">Risks specific to the mode</h2>
    <ul class="space-y-2 text-xs text-slate-400 leading-relaxed list-disc pl-5">
      <li>The pool is the counterparty. Its risk controls, not an order book, determine execution quality.</li>
      <li>Profit share reduces the upside of a winning trade; a 20% share is a material drag on high-turnover strategies.</li>
      <li>Dynamic slippage can dominate the stated fee in volatile or thin markets.</li>
      <li>The zero-fee promotion can end without notice.</li>
      <li>Liquidation follows the mode's mark-price and margin rules; confirm them in the docs before sizing.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="text-[11px] text-slate-400">
      Related: <a href="/aster-dex/1001x/" class="text-sky-400 hover:text-sky-300">1001x and Degen Mode</a> ·
      <a href="/aster-dex/privacy/" class="text-sky-400 hover:text-sky-300">privacy mechanics</a> ·
      <a href="/aster-dex/fees/" class="text-sky-400 hover:text-sky-300">full fee schedule</a>
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="border-t border-[#1e293b]/60 pt-6">
    <p class="text-[11px] text-slate-400">
      Written by <a href="/kirsty-moreland/" class="text-sky-400 hover:text-sky-300">Kirsty Moreland</a> · Technical review by{" "}
      <a href="/about/" class="text-sky-400 hover:text-sky-300">Maksim Sokal</a> ·
      <a href="/disclosure/" class="text-slate-400 hover:text-sky-300">Disclosure</a>
    </p>
  </section>
</AsterLayout>
